// A REPLICATION OF A FROZEN CANDIDATE (U) ON MATCHES NO MODEL OF THIS PROJECT HAS BEEN SCORED ON, WITH A TWO-LOOK SEQUENTIAL TEST. Written 2026-11-28 for docs/CC-CMD-2026-11-27-uefa-forecast-on-tonights-cards.md ("Replication 2026-11-28"), on the
// owner's "Meant ideas 1 and 2": idea 1 the backward holdout on 2024-25 and idea 2 a sequential test in place of one tripwire (proposed as a Wald test and replaced by a two-look test, see CHOICES), two of the five ideas in the assistant's answer to "What novel thinking accomplishes the UEFA forecaster?", listed in outbox/cc-session-2026-11-28-uefa-replication.md. It changes nothing in src/.
//
// THIS FILE, AT THE COMMIT THAT FIXES EACH VERSION OF THE RULE, HOLDS THE RULE AND NO SCORING CODE. This is VERSION 3 (see VERSION in the block). When a version is written, nothing has been scored and no model number on any 2024-25 data exists. The data bundles, the scoring tooling and the runs are
// separate commits made AFTER the commit that fixes the version, each leaving the RULE block below byte-identical (its sha256 is printed by `--print-rule-hash` and recorded in the commit message of the commit that fixes the version).
// DATA AND TOOLING THAT PREDATE THIS VERSION: a recheck bundle of 2026-08-01 to 2026-11-26 (run 46102782008, commit 08703e46) and a structure census of 2024-25 (run 46104147304, commit 2e5238df), both described under VERSION, and the ESPN collector scripts/uefa-replication-data.mjs and its mutation harness were first committed in ef94a1ad (before version 1) and rewritten in b36f19d3 (after version 1, before version 2) to implement the row conditions; b36f19d3 also first committed its workflow. Three census runs executed the collector and printed counts of kinds only:
// 46095464139 (2024-25 window, commit 8a19af6f), 46098677826 (2026-08-01 to 2026-11-26, commit 44410119) and 46100707804 (2026-11-27 to 2026-11-28, commit 37a724eb). They are conformed to this version in later commits: the rule below says what the collector must do, and any later change to it is a change toward this text.
//
//   Today:  node outbox/forecast-replicate-uefa-2026-11-28.mjs --print-rule-hash     (prints the sha256 of the RULE block)
//           node outbox/forecast-replicate-uefa-2026-11-28.mjs --print-rule          (prints the RULE block)
// The hash by hand:  sed -n '/^\/\/ ==== RULE BEGIN$/,/^\/\/ ==== RULE END$/p' outbox/forecast-replicate-uefa-2026-11-28.mjs | head -c -1 | sha256sum     (sed prints a final newline; head -c -1 drops it; `--print-rule` also ends with one).
// This file can be imported (its exports RULE, decide, stopVerdict, look2Gate, ruleBlock, ruleBlockSha256 and MARKER_LINES serve the tests; the scoring tooling does not trust them: it cuts the RULE block from this file's bytes by the recipe above and evaluates that text, G3 (b)); it acts as a command only when it is the entry script.
// LICENCE of the match data (ESPN's public scoreboard) is NOT assessed here (STANDARDS Rule 45): flagged for a human.
import fs from 'node:fs'
import { createHash } from 'node:crypto'
import { fileURLToPath } from 'node:url'

const SELF_PATH = fileURLToPath(import.meta.url)
const sha256 = b => createHash('sha256').update(b).digest('hex')

// ==== RULE BEGIN
// THE REPLICATION RULE FOR CANDIDATE U (2026-11-28), VERSION 3. It is fixed before any 2024-25 match row was written to disk or printed and before any model number was computed on 2024-25 data. A categorical census (see VERSION) read every 2024-25 payload in memory and printed counts of kinds only.
// The author HAS read published AGGREGATES of that season (see SEEN). The block's bytes are the text from the first character of the line that opens the block (the RULE BEGIN marker line) to the last character of the line that closes it (the RULE END marker line) inclusive, UTF-8, LF line endings,
// no trailing newline; the file is ASCII only; each marker line occurs exactly once in the file as a whole line. RULE_COMMIT is the earliest commit on main whose copy of this file contains a block with this sha256: its message holds the line `RULE block sha256: <64 hex>`, and G3 reads the hash from there and from
// git show of the file at that commit. A bundle's data commit message holds the line `bundle sha256: <64 hex> <bytes> bytes <path>`. A repaired bundle is a new file at a new path (a data commit adds each path once), and G3 (a) reads the commit that added that path.
//
// WHY. The pre-registered fit of 2026-11-27 (rule dc9fdce5, RULE sha256 6cf976ba8b895439894346c066c22ff752d2789b208cdccdb563ddae41118cf1, run 46071082308) said DO NOT BUILD because ONE tripwire failed: on the frozen 2026-27 bundle (n 90) U's Brier was 0.0159 above the
//   base rate's (z +0.48). That test could not tell: the standard deviation of the paired difference there was 0.315, so its standard error was 0.033, and a true gain of the cross-validation size (0.032) would have passed it only about 83% of the time. This rule is the NEW DECISION
//   that fit's NO FURTHER LOOK clause reserves ("Any revision after that is a new decision with new matches to read"): the SAME candidate, constants frozen, on new matches, with a sequential test.
//
// THE CANDIDATE.  U exactly as defined in the RULE block of outbox/forecast-fit-uefa-2026-11-27.mjs (sha256 above): rating(club) = ppg + 0.25 * gdpg + 0.10 * gfpg over the club's SCORED league-phase matches in THIS competition and season strictly earlier than the match in the order below (ppg = points per game, 3 for a win, 1 for a draw, 0 for a loss; gdpg = goal difference per game; gfpg = goals for per game; each per game played in those matches);
//   d = rating(home) - rating(away) + home; pDraw = share; pHome = (1 - share) * logistic(d / scale); pAway = 1 - pDraw - pHome. N = 8 / 8 / 6, K = 3 eligibility (both clubs have >= 3 SCORED league-phase matches before the match) and the outcome y (0 home win, 1 draw, 2 away win,
//   from the two scores) are that rule's. CONSTANTS, FROZEN: home 1.34, scale 1.97, share 0.18, the rounded values that run printed. They are not refitted, re-rounded or changed for any reason; no constant is fitted under this rule.
// THE BENCHMARK, FROZEN.  BASE RATE = (122, 43, 69) / 234, the home, draw and away counts of the 234 eligible 2025-26 forecasts of that run, the same three numbers for every forecast at both looks.
//
// THE DATA, AND THE ROW MAPPING (fixed).  Source: ESPN's public scoreboard, https://site.api.espn.com/apis/site/v2/sports/soccer/<slug>/scoreboard?dates=YYYYMMDD, ONE DAY PER READ, slug -> label: uefa.champions -> UEFA Champions League (N 8), uefa.europa -> UEFA Europa League (N 8),
//   uefa.europa.conf -> UEFA Europa Conference League (N 6). Every day of the window is read. A day that does not answer HTTP 200 with a JSON body holding an events array is read once more (after any status other than 200, 403 and 429, a network error, a non-JSON body or a body without an events array) and, if it still does not,
//   stops the collection and writes nothing; a 403 or a 429 is never read again and stops it at once. A missing day is never an empty day.
//   A row is made from an event iff competitions[0].status.type.completed is true. The row has exactly these fields, in this order (FIELDS): id = <label>_<requested day>_e<event id>; sport = the label; date = the REQUESTED day as YYYY-MM-DD; home = String(team.id) of the competitor with homeAway "home";
//   away = String(team.id) of the one with "away" (a CLUB IS ITS ESPN team id; there is no spelling and no alias); home_score and away_score = Number(score text) of the home and the away competitor when the text matches ^[0-9]+$, else null (no lenient parsing; 007 is 7); start_time = the event's date exactly as served; espn_event_id = String(event.id);
//   home_name and away_name = the team's shortDisplayName, else displayName (for a human; no scoring step reads them); phase = the event's season.slug; status = competitions[0].status.type.name. Winner, shootout, aggregate, form, records, advance and statistics fields are never read.
//   A completed event with no event id, or without exactly one home and one away competitor each with a non-empty team id, is COUNTED as skipped and is a G3 failure; it is never silently dropped or guessed. The collector writes, with the rows, per competition: events, completed, nonCompleted, skipped, invalidScore, dateMismatch,
//   the status names and the phases of the rows made (counts; so each excludes skipped events), and in total duplicateEventIds (a repeated event id is kept once and counted); it prints all of these. DATE CHECK: the requested day must equal the UTC day of start_time (Date.parse) or the day before it; a start_time that is absent, unparseable or has no Z or explicit offset fails it (counted as dateMismatch).
//   STATUS: a completed event that is a league-phase match (by the counting rule below) must have the status name STATUS_FULL_TIME, else G3 fails; a completed event that is not a league-phase match is never scored and its status name is only counted (the first census found STATUS_FINAL_AET and STATUS_FINAL_PEN among the completed events and did not cross status by phase; the structure census of 2024-25, see VERSION, crossed them: every league-phase match is STATUS_FULL_TIME).
//   LEAGUE-PHASE COUNTING RULE: a match is a league-phase match iff BOTH clubs have played fewer than N earlier events in that competition's rows of that season; earlier = by (date, Date.parse(start_time), Number(espn_event_id)). An event with a null score counts as an event for this rule and gives no forecast and no rating update (G3 (i) forbids a null score in a league-phase match). A club never has two events on one date, so the order inside a date changes no rating;
//   two events of one club on one date are a G3 failure. season.slug and altGameNote are NOT used to find the league phase; the count of events with phase "league-phase" per competition is printed as a cross-check only. The scoring tooling implements these definitions directly and does not call prepare() of the 2026-11-27 tooling; on the 2025-26 rows its forecasts equal prepare()'s (a committed test), and it is never run on the rows of two seasons together.
//   Within each competition the forecasts are in the order above; pooled sums run over the competitions in the order Champions League, Europa League, Conference League (another order changes a sum only in its last bits).
//   LOOK 1 SET: the 2024-25 competitions, every day 2024-09-01 to 2025-06-30.
//   FORWARD SET: the 2026-27 competitions: every day 2026-08-01 to the day of the run, read by the same collector under the same rules. A 2026-27 league-phase match whose requested day is 2026-11-26 or earlier is a FROZEN match (an INPUT to ratings, never scored under this rule);
//     one whose requested day is 2026-11-27 or later is a FORWARD match (scored). The frozen part of this read must have exactly the espn_event_id set of the pinned frozen bundle outbox/forecast-uefa-data-2026-27-frozen-2026-11-27.json (sha256 3ccdad96a359bbdc6f1e0608058dec23f26a04dcc944817d648594f28130735e,
//     252 ids), compared as sets (both counts and the sizes of both differences are printed); the FRESH READ governs the ratings, and for every frozen id its home score, away score and start time must equal the pinned bundle's (G3 (k)); any difference is a G3 failure.
//
// THE LOOKS (two, and no other).
//   LOOK 1: all ELIGIBLE forecasts of the 2024-25 competitions' league phase, in (date, Date.parse(start_time), Number(espn_event_id)) order. Run once to a completed G3, when the bundle exists, by the workflow uefa-replicate-run.yml (mode look1) on a GitHub runner: the result file records the run id, the checkout sha and the tooling sha, and a second completed result is refused. The result also records the bundle path and sha256 it scored (key bundle24) and the scoring module's sha256; the Look 1 bundle, for every later purpose, is the bundle that result names, and the workflow takes the bundle path as an input.
//   LOOK 2: only if the committed Look 1 verdict is CONTINUE TO LOOK 2. It scores the eligible forecasts of the FORWARD matches (the frozen matches are not scored) and pools them AFTER the Look 1 forecasts. It runs only when every club of the three 2026-27 competitions has played exactly N league-phase matches in the read
//     (396 league-phase matches exist, 252 of them frozen, so the pooled set is the Look 1 set plus the eligible forecasts of the remaining 144), and on no other basis. UEFA's calendar was not read.
//   LOOK 2 GATE. look2Gate(today, state) below is the whole decision to run, wait or stop; today is the UTC date, and a malformed date or count throws. It is carried out by the scheduled workflow uefa-look2-gate.yml, committed BEFORE the Look 1 run, which calls it once a day. The state is read from committed files: state.look1Verdict is the key `verdict` of outbox/forecast-replicate-uefa-look1-result-2026-11-28.json (no file: no verdict);
//     state.look1RecomputeAgrees is the key `agrees` of outbox/forecast-replicate-uefa-look1-recompute-2026-11-28.json (no file: false); state.look2VerdictCommitted is the existence of outbox/forecast-replicate-uefa-look2-result-2026-11-28.json; state.look2Stops and state.look2Repairs are the numbers of stop files (outbox/forecast-replicate-uefa-look2-result-2026-11-28-stop-<n>.txt) and repair records (the same path with -repair-<n>.md) there;
//     state.allClubsOnN is true iff a fresh read of the forward window by the collector gives every club of the three competitions exactly N league-phase matches (396 in all). The gate is INERT unless the Look 1 verdict is CONTINUE TO LOOK 2 and its recomputation record says agrees true. While it is INERT the workflow reads no ESPN data and writes nothing, and it has no manual path that scores anything (a manual dispatch runs only its inert check).
//     Before it says RUN the workflow runs G3 on the freshly read forward bundle, uncounted (an integrity pre-check: a failure is WAIT and costs no stop, so a persistent external failure ends at the deadline with no stop spent). When it says RUN the workflow commits the forward bundle (its sha256 and the scoring module's in the message) and runs Look 2 once on it, with the Look 1 bundle named in the Look 1 result (key bundle24); the Look 2 result records bundle24 and bundle26 (path and sha256 each). DEADLINE 2027-02-15 (UTC): it binds the date a Look 2 run STARTS; a result committed by a run that started on or before it counts; if no Look 2 result is committed by a run that started on or before it, the result is NO VERDICT (the programme is void; any further test of U is a new decision).
// THE STATISTIC (no rounding anywhere).  Per eligible forecast D = Brier(U) - Brier(base); Brier = the sum over the three outcomes of (forecast - indicator)^2 (a uniform guess scores 0.6667). z = mean(D) / (sd(D) / sqrt(n)) with the sample standard deviation (n - 1). NEGATIVE FAVOURS U.
//   "U has skill", in this rule, means only: mean(D) < 0 against this frozen table-free forecast, at the boundary below.
// THE BOUNDARIES.  One-sided total alpha 0.05 split by Bonferroni: LOOK 1 alpha 0.0125, z1 = -2.241402728; LOOK 2 alpha 0.0375, z2 = -1.780464342 (the one-sided normal quantiles rounded to 9 decimals and used as printed; the statistic itself is not rounded). No correction for the correlation of the two looks is claimed; it only makes the test conservative.
// THE GUARDS. G1 and G2 are evaluated only after the boundary is crossed, on the forecasts of that look (at Look 2 the three cells are each competition's Look 1 and forward forecasts pooled); G3 is evaluated FIRST at every look.
//   G1  each of the three competitions on its own: U's paired z against the base rate <= +1.0.
//   G2  the home-win slope, on the forecasts of that look (the pooled set at Look 2): the coefficient on logit(pHome) in the logistic regression of "home win" on [1, logit(pHome)] by Newton's method from (0, 1), at most 100 iterations, each step applied and then its Euclidean norm tested; the fit has converged iff some step within the 100 has norm < 1e-12, and the standard error is the square root of the variance of that coefficient
//     (the second diagonal element, 0-based [1][1], of the inverse observed information at the final point). The slope is within 1.96 standard errors of 1 (equality passes). Non-convergence within 100 iterations is a non-finite slope, and G2 then fails.
//   G3  INTEGRITY, evaluated FIRST at every look and before anything else is computed. FILES: (a), (c) to (j), (l), (m) and (n) apply to each bundle read (the Look 1 bundle; at Look 2 also the forward 2026-27 bundle, where (c) is not applied); (b) applies once; (k) concerns the pinned frozen file, which is exempt from (a) and (l); (o) concerns the Look 1 recomputation record, at Look 2 (its rows have 9 fields and its commit message holds no hash: only its espn_event_ids, scores and start times are used).
//     (a) each bundle file's sha256 equals the one in the commit message of the commit that added that path (this shows the file is unchanged since the workflow committed it, not that the collection was right), and the Look 1 bundle is the first 2024-25 bundle path ever committed or the one a repair record names (a line `bundle24: <path>`); (b) the sha256 of the RULE block text that the tooling itself cuts from the rule file's bytes and executes (never a value the rule file exports) equals the one in the commit message of RULE_COMMIT, the block stored in RULE_COMMIT (git show) has the same sha256 whatever that message says, the block is identical in every commit that touches the rule file from RULE_COMMIT to the checkout, and RULE_COMMIT is an ancestor of the checkout and of the commit that added each bundle;
//     (c) completed events per competition 189 / 189 / 153 for 2024-25 (as read by dry runs on 2026-11-28); (d) 144 / 144 / 108 league-phase matches by the counting rule; (e) every club on exactly 8 / 8 / 6 of them and 36 distinct clubs a competition (clubs counted over all of that competition's rows); (f) duplicateEventIds is 0 as the bundle states it, no espn_event_id repeats among the rows, every espn_event_id matches ^[0-9]+$, and counts.rows equals the number of rows;
//     (g) skipped is 0, no club has two events on one date and no match has one club on both sides; (h) every league-phase match has the row status STATUS_FULL_TIME; (i) no null score in a league-phase match; (j) dateMismatch is 0 as the bundle states it and recomputed from the rows (a start_time with no Z or explicit offset is a mismatch);
//     (k) at Look 2: the frozen bundle file's sha256 equals frozenBundleSha256; the frozen part of the forward read has exactly the 252 espn_event_ids of the pinned bundle; and for each of them the read's home score, away score and start time equal the pinned bundle's; (l) the bundle's fields list is FIELDS, every row has exactly those keys in that order, the bundle's from, to and daysRead are the window's
//     (for the forward bundle `to` is on or after 2026-11-27 and not after the UTC date of the run) and every read answered HTTP 200; (m) the eligible forecasts, counted from the presence of scores only, number 90 / 90 / 54 per competition at Look 1, and the forward matches at Look 2 give 144 eligible forecasts, every forward match being eligible; (n) the scoring module scripts/uefa-replicate-score.mjs (which holds the rule loader, the scoring, the sets that are scored, the Look 2 pool and the verdict call: everything that fixes a number; the run module holds only G3 checks, I/O and reporting) has the sha256 recorded in the commit message of the commit that added each bundle
//     (a line `scoring sha256: <64 hex> scripts/uefa-replicate-score.mjs`) and, at Look 2, the one recorded in the Look 1 result; (o) at Look 2 the Look 1 recomputation record exists, says agrees true, and is about this Look 1 result (its run z and run verdict are the result's). These are computed from the data alone, from the presence of scores and never their values (G3b is the exception: its line shows the Look 1 z and verdict, which are already public): none of them computes a forecast probability, a Brier or a statistic, or prints or keeps an outcome. (d), (e), (g), (h) and (m) are properties of the 2024-25 calendar and were tried on it before this rule was fixed (VERSION).
//   G3b  AT LOOK 2 ONLY, after (a) to (o) hold and before any forward forecast is scored: the Look 1 forecasts are scored again from the Look 1 bundle by the same code; the z must equal the committed Look 1 z (stored as a JSON double, which round-trips exactly) to 1e-12, and decide at Look 1 on the recomputed statistics must give the committed Look 1 verdict, which must be CONTINUE TO LOOK 2 (so an edited verdict key cannot start a Look 2).
//     That number is already public, so this reveals no new outcome; a difference is a G3 failure.
// ORDER OF EVALUATION (outcome-blind failure path).  The tooling evaluates (a) to (o) before it computes anything that depends on an outcome. If any G3 check fails it prints every check as PASS or FAIL, the counts and the line `VERDICT: <stopVerdict(n)> (stop n of 3)`, writes no file containing a computed statistic and exits non-zero; the scoring code is unreachable
//   when G3 fails (shown by a mutation). An `--integrity-only` mode (G3 (a) to (o) for the Look 1 bundle only, no stop counted; its runs, and the repairs they prompt before the first completed run, are neither counted nor bounded, and such a repair is recorded in the session record and not as a `-repair-<n>.md` file) exists. A STOP is one completed run of a look that failed G3; a collector that did not answer, an integrity-only run and a gate that said WAIT are not stops. A stop is not a look and gives no verdict.
//   Stop files and repair records are counted in the tree and in every commit (a deleted file still counts). Each stop writes a stop file `<result path without .json>-stop-<n>.txt`, and the third stop of a look is its NO VERDICT (its result file says so). An exception before a result is written (an unreadable bundle, a missing file) writes nothing, is neither a stop nor a verdict, and exits 3. A look is run once: a printed completed result counts as the look even if it was not committed, and the tooling refuses to run when the result path was ever added to the repository (in the tree or in any commit). The workflow commits and pushes the result (or the stop file) in its own commit BEFORE any recomputation, so a crash in the recomputation cannot lose or repeat a look; a result committed with no recomputation record is UNCONFIRMED (the gate stays INERT, and only the comparison may be run again, on the committed result).
//   A REPAIR is allowed only for a defect in the DATA or the COLLECTION or in a G3 check (never in this rule, a constant, a boundary or the scoring): a re-read of days into a bundle at a new path, or a fix of the collector or of a G3 check shown on synthetic data and committed before the re-run. A repair of a G3 check may only make it stricter or fix a crash on well-formed input, and never touches (b), (n), (o), G3b, the order of evaluation or the verdict path (any such edit is a new decision). A repair is decided from names, dates, ids and counts alone and written to a repair record `<result path without .json>-repair-<n>.md` committed before the next run;
//   every bundle commit is listed in the session record. At most two repairs are made for a look, and a look with a stop that has no repair record yet does not run (at Look 2 the gate says WAIT). No repair or stop decision uses any outcome-bearing number; the forward results are public scores, and the author does not compute Look 2 early.
//   A repair wait is bounded in days only by the Look 2 deadline: inaction can end a look without a verdict and cannot produce a favourable one. "Run once" means once to a completed G3.
// THE VERDICTS (a total table, evaluated in this order; stopVerdict(), decide() and look2Gate() below are it).  0. LOOK 2 DEADLINE, only when the committed Look 1 verdict is CONTINUE TO LOOK 2 and its recomputation record agrees (otherwise the gate is INERT, and with a committed Look 2 result it is DONE): no committed Look 2 result and a date after 2027-02-15 -> NO VERDICT.
//   1. G3 fails at any look -> stopVerdict(n): STOPPED AT G3 (no verdict) at the first and second stop of that look, NO VERDICT at the third (decide() is called only with G3 passed).  2. z is not a finite number (n < 2, sd 0) -> NO VERDICT.
//   3. LOOK 1: z <= z1 -> go to 4; z > z1 -> CONTINUE TO LOOK 2. LOOK 2: z <= z2 -> go to 4; z > z2 -> DO NOT BUILD.  4. G1 and G2 both hold (the three cells are the three competitions, each z a finite number <= 1.0; the slope and its standard error finite, the standard error > 0) -> BUILD; either fails -> DO NOT BUILD (there is no Look 2 after a Look 1 crossing).
//   BUILD means only this: Task 3 of docs/CC-CMD-2026-11-27-uefa-forecast-on-tonights-cards.md may be built with these constants exactly and a method string that carries them and names this rule. The line is pull-only (Rule F) and is shown only for eligible matches (U has no prior). BUILD does not retire the frozen 2026-27 bundle's adverse out-of-fit result
//     (+0.0159 Brier, n 90, z +0.48), which neither look includes and which is reported beside any BUILD.
// WHICH NUMBER GOVERNS.  The run's printed numbers govern, and a look's committed result is never rewritten. An independent recomputation of each look is a check, made by the same workflow run that produced the result, AFTER the result is committed (scripts/uefa-replicate-run.mjs --compare-independent against scripts/uefa-replicate-independent.mjs), and committed as the record outbox/forecast-replicate-uefa-look<L>-recompute-2026-11-28.json.
//   The independent implementation is written by a separate agent from THIS text and the frozen definitions alone, never from the run's code, and is committed before the first bundle. Its contract: `node scripts/uefa-replicate-independent.mjs --look 1 --bundle24 <path>` or `--look 2 --bundle24 <path> --bundle26 <path>` writes exactly one JSON object to stdout (logs to stderr) with the keys verdict (one of the verdict strings) and z (a number, or null when not finite) and exits 0;
//   anything else is a crash, which leaves the look UNCONFIRMED. The record has the keys agrees (the two verdicts are equal), zAgrees (the z values agree to 1e-9), finalVerdict (the run's verdict when agrees is true, else NO VERDICT: this is what a consumer of the verdict reads), both z values and verdicts, and the sha256 of the independent script. Before the first bundle is committed the independent implementation must agree to 1e-9 with the run's tooling
//   on the committed synthetic fixtures outbox/uefa-replication-synthetic-*.json (written by scripts/export-uefa-replicate-fixtures.mjs, reproducible byte for byte; their sha256 are in the message of the commit that adds them) and reproduce the two committed known answers (the 2026-11-27 fit's frozen-bundle result and the 2025-26 outcome counts; those two bundles carry club names, which the alias map CLUB_ALIASES of outbox/forecast-fit-uefa-2026-11-27.mjs maps, for these two known answers only);
//   its test, scripts/test-uefa-replicate-independent.mjs, prints the result. A look's verdict stands only when its record says agrees true: a record that says agrees false makes that look NO VERDICT (the result file remains the record of what the run printed, and the look is not repeated or repaired); a z difference above 1e-9 with the same verdict is recorded (zAgrees false) and does not void the verdict.
//   The Look 2 gate is INERT without an agreeing Look 1 record, and G3 (o) refuses a Look 2 without one. After a bundle is committed the tooling changes only by a repair of the collection or of a G3 check; the scoring module never changes, and G3 (n) enforces it; the independent implementation changes only to fix a crash, shown on the fixtures. Neither number is ever chosen because it is the favourable one.
// BLIND UNTIL THE VERDICT.  The author opens no 2024-25 row before the Look 1 verdict and prints none; the bundle is committed by a workflow, not by hand; the session record lists every command that touches it. THIS IS A DISCIPLINE, NOT A MACHINE-ENFORCED CONTROL: the bundle is an ordinary readable file.
// NO FURTHER LOOK.  Look 1 and Look 2 are the only looks. If Look 1 crosses its boundary, Look 2 is not run and the forward matches are NEVER scored under this rule (they stay unspent for any later candidate). No scoring on any set with a changed constant, K, weight, boundary, set, order or candidate; no alternative candidate, K or benchmark is scored on 2024-25, 2025-26 or the frozen 2026-27 bundle under this rule.
